          "id": "tokyo_item_2",
          "type": "ListItem",
          "properties": {
            "primaryText": "Conditions: July in Tokyo is characterized by high heat combined with oppressive humidity. This creates a high heat index, making the air feel thick, heavy, and difficult to breathe."
          }
        },
        {
          "id": "tokyo_item_3",
          "type": "ListItem",
          "properties": {
            "primaryText": "Impact on Asthma: Hot, humid air is a common and potent trigger for asthma. It can irritate airways, lead to inflammation, and cause bronchospasm (the tightening of muscles around the airways), making an asthma attack more likely. The high moisture content also promotes the growth of mold, another potential allergen."
          }
        },
